This project builds on and redistributes patches for the following
third-party works. Their own licenses govern their respective code.

1. huggingface/speech-to-speech
   https://github.com/huggingface/speech-to-speech
   License: Apache License 2.0
   Not vendored here — `setup.sh` clones and pins it at a specific commit.
   `patches/` contains an overlay pack of modified files from this framework
   (see patches/README.md for exactly which files and why).

2. met4citizen/TalkingHead
   https://github.com/met4citizen/TalkingHead
   License: MIT
   The webclient's avatar rendering code under `webclient/avatar/vendor/`
   integrates with this library.

3. Bundled avatar heads (webclient/avatar/model/*.glb)
   Twelve example heads ship. They are NOT uniformly licensed — see
   webclient/avatar/model/LICENSE-NOTE.txt for the per-file terms:
   - Six are redistributed from the met4citizen/TalkingHead repository,
     mirroring its own public distribution: mpfb.glb (CC0, public domain);
     brunette.glb and brunette-t.glb (Ready Player Me, CC BY-NC 4.0);
     avatarsdk.glb (AvatarSDK), avaturn.glb (Avaturn) and vroid.glb
     (VRoid Studio), each for non-commercial use.
   - Six were generated for this project (old-man, young-woman,
     heavyset-neutral, professional-woman, young-man, elder-woman) from
     MakeHuman Community asset packs declared CC0; the mesh, morph and
     texture content is CC0, and the embedded rig derives from the
     TalkingHead project's MPFB rig (MIT, attributed here).
   The MIT License in LICENSE does not cover these assets. For any
   non-personal use, check each head's terms or replace it with one you
   have rights to.

4. Vendored libraries (webclient/avatar/vendor/)
   - three.js (MIT) — 3D rendering.
   - met4citizen/TalkingHead modules (MIT) — 3D head render + lip-sync glue,
     with small local patches marked LOCAL VENDOR PATCH inline (meshopt decoder wiring and
     the upstream armature-root fallback).
   - HeadAudio by Mika Suominen (MIT, see its LICENSE) — real-time
     audio-driven viseme detection (webclient/avatar/vendor/headaudio/).

5. Fonts (webclient/themes/fonts/)
   Cinzel — SIL Open Font License (see OFL.txt alongside the font files).

6. Downloaded at install or first run — NOT redistributed here
   Fetched from their own sources onto the user's machine, under their own
   licences:
   - PyTorch (torch, torchaudio), CPU wheels — BSD-3-Clause.
   - nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3 (speech-to-text weights) — CC-BY-4.0.
   - kyutai/pocket-tts-without-voice-cloning (text-to-speech weights) —
     CC-BY-4.0. Optional: kyutai/pocket-tts (clone-capable, gated) —
     CC-BY-4.0.
   - snakers4/silero-vad (voice activity detection) — MIT.
   - Optional: openWakeWord — code Apache-2.0; its pre-trained models,
     including hey_jarvis, are CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (non-commercial).
   SETUP.md step 0 lists sizes and where each lands.

Theme reference images and the 2D still-avatar source image used during
development are NOT redistributed (see .gitignore) — supply your own image
for the 2D avatar path. Nothing in this NOTICE grants rights to any asset
not present in the repository.

